# Fused whole-struct internal read whole into an output — refused (Direction B)

The FUSION (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3a, 2026-08-25) inlines a whole-struct per-element
map INTERNAL only where it is consumed as bare per-field reads: the struct list
never exists on the wire. Here `shares` IS consumed per field (the `totaal`
fold), but ALSO read WHOLE into the output `picked` (`definition picked equals
shares`) — the exact Direction B case: a caller could read the whole list, which
has no clingo image. The fused internal is excluded from `vars`, so this read
refuses loudly rather than crashing on the absent entry (the lens flank).

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag + 100

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  internal shares content list of Kamer
  output totaal content integer
  output picked content list of Kamer

scope Aanslag:
  definition shares equals
    map each g among grondslagen to
    (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: g })
  definition totaal equals
    sum integer of map each s among shares to s.bedrag
  definition picked equals shares
```
